## 1. Project Overview & Part 1 Feedback Corrections

KZN Collectibles & TCG is a hobby and collectibles store that focuses on trading cards, games and related accessories. This repository contains the front-end website that I created to display the products, provide information about the store and allow customers to register for events.

### Part 1 Feedback Corrections

Based on the feedback from Part 1, I made a few changes to improve the structure of the website:

- I made sure that the pages use the correct semantic HTML elements, such as `<header>`, `<main>` and `<article>`, instead of relying too much on `<div>` elements.
- I added the external stylesheet link to all five pages using `<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/styles.css">`. This makes sure that the CSS is correctly connected to each HTML page for Part 2.

---

## 2. Website Goals

The main goals of the KZN Collectibles & TCG website are:

- To make the store's products easier for customers to view online, with a target of 1,500+ catalogue views per month.
- To make tournament and event registrations easier by allowing customers to sign up online, with a target of 40+ tournament registrations per month.

---

## 3. Sitemap & Page Structure

The website consists of five main pages:

- **`index.html`** – The home page includes a hero section, information about the latest card expansions and updates about upcoming tournaments.
- **`about.html`** – This page gives some background about the store, its history, community standards and staff.
- **`products.html`** – Displays the different products available, including sealed trading cards, accessories and games.
- **`enquiry.html`** – Allows customers to make tournament enquiries or ask about sourcing specific cards.
- **`contact.html`** – Provides the store's contact information for the PMB Flagship and Hilton Express branches, as well as a feedback form.

---

## 4. Part 2: CSS & Responsive Layout

For Part 2, I focused on improving the overall design of the website and making sure that it works properly on different screen sizes.

- **External Stylesheet:** I created a `styles.css` file and used CSS variables in `:root` to keep the main colours of the website consistent. The main colours are Obsidian Black and Crimson Red.
- **Layout:** I used Flexbox for the navigation and CSS Grid for the product section. The grid uses `auto-fit` and `minmax()` so that the products can adjust depending on the available screen size.
- **Typography:** I used relative units such as `rem` and suitable line heights to make the text easier to read on different devices.
- **Pseudo-Classes:** I added `:hover`, `:focus` and `:active` states to make the website more interactive, especially for product cards and form fields.
- **Responsive Design:** I added media queries for desktop, tablet and mobile screen sizes. The product layout changes from multiple columns to a single-column layout on smaller smartphone screens.

